<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Android 12+ backup/transfer rules (Google Play's "safe data transfer to a
    new device" quality requirement, 2026). WHITELIST mode: the moment a
    section has one <include>, everything not included is out — any NEW
    persistence layer someone adds later stays device-local until it is
    deliberately listed here (mirror of DataEraser's explicit-list policy).

    What transfers and why:
      - sshai.db (+ -wal)      Room: server rows, key METADATA (public half,
                               fingerprint), chat bookkeeping. The user's
                               actual belongings. The -wal file rides along so
                               a restore sees the last committed state, not a
                               possibly-stale checkpoint.
      - datastore/settings     Preferences the user tuned by hand.
      - datastore/auth_methods Which auth method each server uses — metadata,
                               not credentials.

    What NEVER leaves the device (SEC-7, INVARIANTS.md) — everything below is
    kept out BY the whitelist (lint forbids a redundant <exclude> for a path
    no <include> covers, so the whitelist itself is the exclusion):
      - encrypted_servers.xml  Passwords, private-key PEMs, passphrases. The
                               keyset is wrapped by an Android-Keystore master
                               key that cannot leave this device's hardware —
                               a copy is undecryptable garbage anywhere else.
                               SecretsStore self-heals if an OEM migration
                               tool copies it around our rules.
      - session_history cache  Chat bodies stay off Google's servers; they
                               re-sync from the user's own server on demand.
      - agent/sessions/upload caches — device-local, rebuilt on first use.

    cloud-backup additionally requires client-side encryption
    (disableIfNoEncryptionCapabilities): server addresses only ever reach a
    cloud backup end-to-end encrypted with the device lockscreen secret.
    device-transfer has no such gate — it is a direct, locally-encrypted
    channel between the user's own two devices.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup disableIfNoEncryptionCapabilities="true">
        <include domain="database" path="sshai.db"/>
        <include domain="database" path="sshai.db-wal"/>
        <include domain="file" path="datastore/settings.preferences_pb"/>
        <include domain="file" path="datastore/auth_methods.preferences_pb"/>
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <include domain="database" path="sshai.db"/>
        <include domain="database" path="sshai.db-wal"/>
        <include domain="file" path="datastore/settings.preferences_pb"/>
        <include domain="file" path="datastore/auth_methods.preferences_pb"/>
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
